<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miro, King of the Suebi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 583</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miro was king of the Suebi in Gallaecia from 570 to 583. A Catholic ruler, he supported the church reforms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-braga">Martin of Braga</a> and the Second Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bracara-augusta">Braga</a> in 572. Drawn into the conflicts of the Visigothic kingdom, he died in 583 during the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, and two years later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> annexed his kingdom.</p></div>
